    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d940">

                <pb facs="0729" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13610.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-27T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 27, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. My October 14, 10 p.m., No. 187. Notwithstanding that the Convention had
                    authorized Carranza to grant the guaranties desired by the Department, I have
                    just received a note from the Acting Secretary for Foreign Affairs in which,
                    after having enumerated the Department’s requests,<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d940-f1"/> he says:</p>
                <p>[Text of part of the note; see the complete text in the next paper.] Translation
                    of the note will follow in the mail tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d940-f1" n="67" xml:id="d940-f1-content">
                <p>As conveyed by the Brazilian Minister in his note of October 8 embodying the
                    Department’s telegram No. 281 of October 7, 5 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
